---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Methodology | nursinghomeneglectcalc.com';
const description = 'How the nursing home neglect damages calculator works: harm type baselines, elder abuse statute enhancement, and punitive damages.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p><em>Reviewed by Aspen Lockwood (AL), Editor-in-Chief. Updated May 2026.</em></p>
  <h2>Pain and suffering baselines</h2><p>By harm type (medians from published nursing home neglect verdicts): pressure sore stage 3/4: $80K; fall with fracture: $60K; malnutrition/dehydration: $50K; medication error: $70K; physical/sexual abuse: $150K; wrongful death: $300K. The higher of the baseline or 3× medical costs is used.</p>
  <h2>Elder abuse statute enhancement</h2><p>States with enhanced elder abuse civil remedies (California, Florida, Texas, Illinois) allow additional damages, attorney fees, and sometimes easier burden of proof. The calculator applies a 1.5× multiplier to pain and suffering when an elder abuse statute is available — reflecting the published premium in verdicts from those states.</p>
  <h2>Punitive damages</h2><p>Available for intentional or reckless (not merely negligent) conduct. Estimated at 1.0× pain and suffering for intentional cases, reflecting median punitive-to-compensatory ratios in published elder abuse verdicts.</p>
</BaseLayout>
